{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Make Emergency Adrenaline Auto-Injectors Available in Public Venues",
        "additional_details": "Anaphylaxis is a life-threatening allergic reaction that can occur within minutes. Not everyone experiencing anaphylaxis has access to their prescribed auto-injector, may require more than one dose or people may experience a severe reaction for the first time without knowing they have an allergy. Having emergency adrenaline auto-injectors available in public venues, alongside trained staff, could help save lives and improve safety for millions of people living with allergies across the UK.",
        "background": "Allow and require public venues, including restaurants, shopping centres, leisure centres, entertainment venues and community spaces to hold emergency adrenaline auto-injectors and ensure staff receive basic anaphylaxis awareness training.",
